# Optional, and only useful on the deploy host. A fine-grained or classic token
# with `public_repo` read scope raises the GitHub API limit from 60 req/hr per
# IP to 5000/hr. Two things read it:
#
#   - /api/github-releases (runtime), which the release-notes page fetches;
#   - content/release-notes.mdx, whose TOC is built at BUILD time — so the
#     variable has to be available during a deploy, not just at runtime.
#
# Without it the site still works, but on a pooled build IP the request can
# come back as a 403 rate-limit body instead of an array, and the TOC silently
# degrades to the page heading alone.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
